<title>INDIA: Indian gold, silver trims early gains, end steady.</title>
<headline>Indian gold, silver trims early gains, end steady.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold and silver opened firm on Tuesday but sluggish physical demand capped early gains towards the close, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Arrivals of smuggled metal was low due to frequent seizures but constant supply through official channels trimmed early gains,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>The trading volume was low and the market moved in a narrow price band, he said.</p>
<p>Gold biscuits (116.50 gramme) settled 150 rupees lower at 59,450 rupees per piece. They were down by 100 rupees per piece on Monday.  </p>
